From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] target/mips: use MIPS indefinite result for invalid L conversions

MIPS CVT.L and fixed-rounding L conversions return the signed 64-bit
indefinite value on Invalid. QEMU's generic helper constant is INT64_MAX,
which is not the architectural result used by the RTL reference contract.

---
 target/mips/tcg/fpu_helper.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/target/mips/tcg/fpu_helper.c b/target/mips/tcg/fpu_helper.c
--- a/target/mips/tcg/fpu_helper.c
+++ b/target/mips/tcg/fpu_helper.c
@@ -37,3 +37,4 @@
 /* SOC_REF_FPU_INT32_INDEFINITE: MIPS invalid W conversion result. */
 #define FP_TO_INT32_OVERFLOW 0x80000000
-#define FP_TO_INT64_OVERFLOW 0x7fffffffffffffffULL
+/* SOC_REF_FPU_INT64_INDEFINITE: MIPS invalid L conversion result. */
+#define FP_TO_INT64_OVERFLOW 0x8000000000000000ULL
